DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T193000
DTSTAMP:20260513T194008
CREATED:20260407T185813Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260407T193317Z
UID:6332-1778695200-1778700600@www.petalumamuseum.com
SUMMARY:Petaluma's past: How to search newspapers.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate National Historic Preservation Month by learning to search Newspapers.com for stories about your family\, your house\, and Petaluma’s colorful past. Discover tips for finding hidden treasures in our historical Argus-Courier and other local newspapers. Bring your own laptop or borrow one of ours and you must register. \nDate:  Wednesday May 13\, 6:00-7:30 PM\nVenue:  Petaluma Regional Library\n100 Fairgrounds Drive\nPetaluma\, CA 94952\nPlease Register Here: Petaluma’s Past: How to search newspapers.com\n(Please register at the bottom of the page)\nOnly 20 seats.  You must register.\n \nConnie Williams from the Petaluma Public Library will guide participants through the Newspapers.com application\, available as part of a Sonoma County Library subscription. Attendees will learn how to access the library’s resources and develop skills for searching local historical newspapers. The event will take place in the newly renovated Petaluma History Room at the Petaluma Regional Library. \n \nFor questions\, contact Connie Williams at cwilliams@sonomalibrary.org \n 
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/petalumas-past-how-to-search-newspapers-com/
LOCATION:Petaluma Regional Library\, 100 Fairgrounds Dr\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952
CATEGORIES:Event,History Trails Walks,Lectures,NHPM
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Newspaper-Article-image.jpg
END:VEVENT
