UID:event_314491946@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260514T023945Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T074500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T080500
SUMMARY:Inner Body Guided-Meditation 
DESCRIPTION:The Mindful Stream (CA)\n"Awareness of the inner body takes you beyond the mind." - Eckhart Tolle\n\nIn this mediation session we will bring our attention here: to the inner body where we practise presence by focusing on our physical sensations.\n\nSessions are suitable for newcomers\, those experienced in Tolle's teachings and anyone wishing to remain completely anonymous. They will last around 20 minutes and cameras and microphones will be disabled. (Depending on the situation\, a free discussion may be held at the end with mics and cameras allowed.)\n\nSessions are suitable for newcomers\, those experienced in Tolle's teachings and anyone wishing to remain completely anonymous. They will last around 20 minutes and cameras and microphones will be disabled. (Depending on the situation\, a free discussion may be held at the end with mics and cameras allowed.)\n\nSee you there!\n\nEmrys also organises a free Work of Byron Katie online mediation group. Visit [this Meetup Group link](https://www.meetup.com/thework-runsfree/) for more information.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/mindfulnesspetaluma/events/314491946/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260426T151455Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260426T151455Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/b/7/0/600_523867024.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Petaluma Museum": "https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/insect-discovery-lab/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:petaluma_museum
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T110000
DTSTAMP:20260513T194009
CREATED:20260428T200310Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T200310Z
UID:6431-1778925600-1778929200@www.petalumamuseum.com
SUMMARY:Insect Discovery Lab
DESCRIPTION:Explore the small but mighty creatures of the wetlands and other ecosystems!\n\nSaturday\, May 16 10:00am – 11:00 am\nPlease Make Your Reservations Here\n\n\nIn connection with Time & Tide: An Artful Exploration of Petaluma’s Wetlands\, the Petaluma Wetlands Alliance invites families to a special hands-on program exploring the small but mighty creatures of the wetlands and other ecosystems. \nJoin educators from SaveNature.org for a free Insect Discovery Lab on Saturday\, May 16\, from 10–11 AM at the Shollenberger Park Gathering Circle. \nSan Francisco–based SaveNature is dedicated to inspiring awareness and participation in the preservation of fragile ecosystems through direct engagement with the natural world. \nYoung explorers will discover the fascinating world of arthropods while meeting beetles\, millipedes\, hissing cockroaches\, walking sticks\, and more. This interactive experience introduces budding scientists to the incredible diversity of insects in our wetlands—and their essential role in the web of life. \nSpace limited to 25 children with parents. Grades K–12. RSVP required.
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/insect-discovery-lab/
LOCATION:Shollenberger Park\, 1400 Cader Lane\, Petaluma\, 94954\, United States
CATEGORIES:Current Exhibit,Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Insect-Discovery-Labs.webp
END:VEVENT
