SUMMARY:SRJC Bands: Pandora's Box
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T220000
DTSTAMP:20250916T151908Z
UID:20260517T023000Z-10078@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T193000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,752,752/621_cs_-_Bands_pandoras-box-1920x1080-LC.rev
 .1778192029.jpg
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:SRJC Symphonic Band &amp\; Jazz Band explore humanity's impact
  on the planet in a concert featuring video projections\, Erik Johnson &am
 p\; Jazz Mirage.  SRJC Symphonic Band and Jazz Band present a powerful mul
 timedia concert exploring humanity\, community\, and our impact on the wor
 ld around us.  Through music and video projections by Nancy Hayashibara\, 
 the program examines questions of identity\, environmental responsibility\
 , division\, and connection. Who are we as a country? Is there room for ev
 eryone? Can we come together as a community in the face of violence\, raci
 sm\, and conflict?  This one-of-a-kind performance invites audiences to re
 flect on the challenges of our time through music\, imagery\, and artistic
  collaboration.  7pm - Preshow with Jazz Mirage.Buy tickets here! (https:/
 /www.eventbrite.com/e/srjc-bands-pandoras-box-wvideo-projections-erik-john
 son-jazz-mirage-tickets-1986100939374)&#160\;View the music department's e
 vents list here. (https://music.santarosa.edu/events)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260508T173514Z
LOCATION:Burbank Auditorium - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/10078-srjc-bands-pandoras-box
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  SRJC Symphonic Band &amp\; Jazz Band exp
 lore humanity's impact on the planet in a concert featuring video projecti
 ons\, Erik Johnson &amp\; Jazz Mirage.</p><p>  SRJC Symphonic Band and Jaz
 z Band present a powerful multimedia concert exploring humanity\, communit
 y\, and our impact on the world around us.</p><p>  Through music and video
  projections by Nancy Hayashibara\, the program examines questions of iden
 tity\, environmental responsibility\, division\, and connection. Who are w
 e as a country? Is there room for everyone? Can we come together as a comm
 unity in the face of violence\, racism\, and conflict?</p><p>  This one-of
 -a-kind performance invites audiences to reflect on the challenges of our 
 time through music\, imagery\, and artistic collaboration.</p><p>  7pm - P
 reshow with Jazz Mirage.</p><p><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/srjc-
 bands-pandoras-box-wvideo-projections-erik-johnson-jazz-mirage-tickets-198
 6100939374" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy tickets here!</a>&#160\;</p
 ><p><a href="https://music.santarosa.edu/events" target="_blank" rel="noop
 ener">View the music department's events list here.</a></p>
