X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Petaluma Arts Center": "https://petalumaartscenter.org/events-exhibitions/origin-stories-symposium"}
X-SOURCE-ID:petaluma_arts_center
SUMMARY:The Origin Stories Symposium
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T160000
UID:d8e20409018f3f1abd6b330cad21068a@petalumaartscenter.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/66
 c6495e2b6d0959e53eb16c/1776398256314-KGYUZXNVCI4P8I8NJ6T7/Amy+McFarland.jp
 eg
DESCRIPTION:$15 Adults\, Children under 10 are free The Origin Stories Sym
 posium is for artists and storytellers of all kinds to celebrate the power
  of human connection.&nbsp\; It's a celebration of empathy and the ways cr
 eativity can open us up to the people we pass on the street every day.&nbs
 p\; The event includes panel discussions\, live music\, and time to explor
 e the art boxes&nbsp\; on display\, illustrating their creators' personal 
 origins. Participants: Jason Chu\, rapper\, activist\, musician\, speaks o
 f hope and healing in a hurting world. As a kid in suburban Delaware\, he 
 found a vocabulary for identity and liberation in hip-hop culture. He is a
 lso a prominent voice in the national Asian American conversation. Sean Ca
 llery\, tv/film composer\, has received 17 Emmy nominations and 4 wins\, p
 lacing him among the most nominated composers of all time. Known for his d
 ynamic and evocative scores\, he has crafted music for celebrated series s
 uch as&nbsp\;Homeland\, &nbsp\;R.J. Decker\,&nbsp\;The Beast in Me\,&nbsp\
 ;the Sherlock Holmes series&nbsp\;Elementary\, Marvel’s&nbsp\;Jessica Jo
 nes\,&nbsp\;Bones\, and&nbsp\;Designated Survivor\, among others.&nbsp\; T
 omo Moriwaki\, teacher and game designer\, got his start at Treyarch. A ga
 me designer for most of his career\, leading the design for Spider-Man: Th
 e Movie Game (2001)\, Spider-Man 2: The Movie Game (2004)\, Boom Blox (200
 8)\, and Medal of Honor (2010). He is the Cofounder and Design Director at
  Hyperkinetic Studios since 2014. There will also be a panel with educator
  Jennifer Jervis and our artist/storyteller guests. #block-e7fe2953e033701
 b8e4f { } #block-e7fe2953e033701b8e4f .sqs-html-content { } #block-e7fe295
